<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arsacid dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Arsacid</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Arsacid dynasty was the ruling family of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthian Empire</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsaces-i">Arsaces I</a> in the third century BCE. It ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> through a relatively decentralised system relying on powerful noble families and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> kings. It was overthrown by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardashir-i">Ardashir I</a> in 224 CE, giving way to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>, although branches continued to rule <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arsacid-dynasty.jpg" alt="Arsacid dynasty" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original file by Ro4444, edited by me · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Parthian_Empire_under_Mithridates_II.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
